{
  "info": {
    "name": "Hyperwake Engine",
    "description": "Omarchy computers on your own machine, over HTTP.\n\n**Setup**\n\n1. Run `npx hyperwake` (or `node bin/hyperwake.js start`). It prints an API URL and a token.\n2. Import the matching environment file, or set the collection variables `baseUrl` and `token` below.\n3. Run **Create machine** first \u2014 it saves the new id into `{{machineId}}` automatically, so every other request just works.\n\n**Order that tells the whole story**\n\nCreate machine \u2192 Get machine (poll until `status` is `ready`) \u2192 Exec \u2192 Write file \u2192 Read file \u2192 Screenshot \u2192 Open desktop \u2192 Stop \u2192 Delete.\n\nOr press **Run** on the `Walkthrough` folder and watch it do all of that with assertions.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{token}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://127.0.0.1:4141",
      "description": "Printed by the engine on start. No trailing slash."
    },
    {
      "key": "token",
      "value": "",
      "description": "Printed by the engine on start; also in ~/.hyperwake/token"
    },
    {
      "key": "machineId",
      "value": "",
      "description": "Filled in by Create machine. You should not need to set this by hand."
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Walkthrough",
      "description": "Run this folder top to bottom. Every request asserts something, so a red result is a real failure rather than a formatting difference.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "0 \u00b7 Auth is enforced",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('an unauthenticated request is refused', () => {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(401);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Sent deliberately without a token. A 401 here is the pass condition."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "1 \u00b7 Discover the API",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('the engine describes itself', () => {",
                  "  const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(body.service).to.eql('hyperwake-engine');",
                  "  pm.expect(body.endpoints).to.be.an('object');",
                  "});",
                  "console.log('host:', JSON.stringify(pm.response.json().host));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Returns the endpoint map and what this host can do \u2014 platform, arch, accelerator."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "2 \u00b7 Create machine",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('created', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "const created = pm.response.json().data;",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('machineId', created.id);",
                  "// An active environment shadows collection variables, so set it there too.",
                  "if (pm.environment.name) pm.environment.set('machineId', created.id);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('readyTries', 0);",
                  "console.log('machine', created.id, '->', created.status);",
                  "pm.test('a fresh machine starts out booting', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(['booting', 'starting', 'ready']).to.include(created.status);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"postman\",\n  \"vcpus\": 4,\n  \"memory_mb\": 4096,\n  \"disk_gb\": 40\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/machines",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "machines"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Creates a **fresh Omarchy instance** and starts it. Every field is optional; the defaults are the body shown.\n\nThe new id is saved to `{{machineId}}` for the rest of the collection."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "3 \u00b7 Wait until ready",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const current = pm.response.json().data;",
                  "console.log('status:', current.status);",
                  "const tries = Number(pm.collectionVariables.get('readyTries') || 0) + 1;",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('readyTries', tries);",
                  "",
                  "// `ready` means the guest reported in for *this* boot and its shell works,",
                  "// not merely that a process started. Poll until then.",
                  "if (current.status === 'ready') {",
                  "  pm.test('reached ready', () => pm.expect(current.status).to.eql('ready'));",
                  "  pm.test('the guest reported its capabilities', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(current.capabilities).to.be.an('object');",
                  "  });",
                  "} else if (tries > 40) {",
                  "  pm.test('reached ready', () => { throw new Error('still ' + current.status + ' after 40 polls'); });",
                  "} else {",
                  "  // pm.execution is the modern API; postman.* is the fallback for older runners.",
                  "  const again = '3 \u00b7 Wait until ready';",
                  "  if (pm.execution && pm.execution.setNextRequest) pm.execution.setNextRequest(again);",
                  "  else postman.setNextRequest(again);",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/machines/{{machineId}}",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "machines",
                "{{machineId}}"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Re-runs itself until `status` is `ready` \u2014 usually six to ten seconds.\n\nStatuses: `booting`, `ready`, `stopped`, and `unknown`. **`unknown` is a real answer**: it means the runtime cannot see the machine, which is not the same as the machine having stopped."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "4 \u00b7 Exec \u2014 prove it is Omarchy",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const shell = pm.response.json().data;",
                  "console.log(shell.stdout);",
                  "pm.test('command succeeded', () => pm.expect(shell.exit_code).to.eql(0));",
                  "pm.test('it is really Arch Linux ARM', () => pm.expect(shell.stdout).to.include('Arch Linux ARM'));",
                  "pm.test('Hyprland is running', () => pm.expect(shell.stdout).to.match(/Hyprland/));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"action\": \"exec\",\n  \"command\": \"grep PRETTY /etc/os-release; uname -m; pgrep -a Hyprland | head -1\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/machines/{{machineId}}/actions",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "machines",
                "{{machineId}}",
                "actions"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Runs a shell command over SSH as `dev`. Returns `exit_code`, `stdout`, `stderr`, plus `timed_out` and `truncated` so you can tell a slow command from a quiet one."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "5 \u00b7 Write a file",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const written = pm.response.json().data;",
                  "pm.test('written', () => pm.expect(written.bytes_written).to.be.above(0));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"action\": \"write_file\",\n  \"path\": \"~/hello.txt\",\n  \"content\": \"round trip\\n\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/machines/{{machineId}}/actions",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "machines",
                "{{machineId}}",
                "actions"
              ]
            },
            "description": "`~` expands in the guest. Parent directories are created."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "6 \u00b7 Read it back",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const file = pm.response.json().data;",
                  "const text = Buffer.from(file.content_base64, 'base64').toString('utf8');",
                  "console.log('content:', JSON.stringify(text));",
                  "pm.test('exact bytes preserved, trailing newline included', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(text).to.eql('round trip\\n');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"action\": \"read_file\",\n  \"path\": \"~/hello.txt\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/machines/{{machineId}}/actions",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "machines",
                "{{machineId}}",
                "actions"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Returns `content_base64` and `size`. Base64 because a file is bytes, not text \u2014 the trailing newline is the byte a file API most often loses.\n\nFiles over 1 MiB are refused; use `exec` to select a smaller portion."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "7 \u00b7 Screenshot",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const shot = pm.response.json().data;",
                  "pm.test('a PNG came back', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(shot.mime_type).to.eql('image/png');",
                  "  pm.expect(shot.image_base64.length).to.be.above(1000);",
                  "});",
                  "console.log('png bytes (base64):', shot.image_base64.length);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"action\": \"screenshot\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/machines/{{machineId}}/actions",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "machines",
                "{{machineId}}",
                "actions"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Captures the guest's screen over its VNC socket. Returns `mime_type` and `image_base64`."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "8 \u00b7 Open the desktop",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const desktop = pm.response.json().data;",
                  "pm.test('the ticket travels in the URL fragment', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(desktop.desktop_url).to.include('/desktop#t=');",
                  "});",
                  "console.log('OPEN THIS IN A BROWSER:');",
                  "console.log(desktop.desktop_url);",
                  "console.log('(single use, ' + desktop.expires_in + 's)');"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/machines/{{machineId}}/desktop",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "machines",
                "{{machineId}}",
                "desktop"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Mints a browser URL for the screen. **Copy it from the Postman console and open it in a browser** to see the live Omarchy desktop.\n\nThe ticket sits in the URL *fragment*, which browsers never send to a server \u2014 so it stays out of access logs and `Referer` headers. Single use, sixty seconds."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "9 \u00b7 Stop",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('accepted', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "console.log('status:', pm.response.json().data.status);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"force\": false\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/machines/{{machineId}}/stop",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "machines",
                "{{machineId}}",
                "stop"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Asks the guest to shut down. `{\"force\": true}` cuts power instead \u2014 faster, and the guest gets no say."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "10 \u00b7 Delete",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('deleted', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('machineId', '');",
                  "if (pm.environment.name) pm.environment.set('machineId', '');"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "DELETE",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/machines/{{machineId}}",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "machines",
                "{{machineId}}"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Stops the machine if it is still running, then destroys it and its disk.\n\nIf the teardown fails, the machine stays registered and you get a 502 saying why \u2014 a delete that cannot remove a machine must not quietly forget it."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "11 \u00b7 Nothing left behind",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const machines = pm.response.json().data;",
                  "console.log('machines remaining:', machines.length);",
                  "pm.test('no leftovers from this run', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(machines.filter((m) => m.name === 'postman')).to.have.length(0);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/machines",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "machines"
              ]
            },
            "description": "The check that matters. A lifecycle that leaves a machine behind has not worked, however green the earlier steps look."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
